From 4ec191d580d44d21ee437c5b1ac1bd5a179dd7f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 23:03:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] res: validate Lua bytecode before parsing and running it

Lua bytecode reaches the client as .lub files inside a GRF. Prototype counts
were trusted, so a 20 byte file could request an 8 GiB allocation or a negative
length; nesting was unbounded, so a few hundred kilobytes overflowed the
goroutine stack unrecoverably; the fallback interpreter indexed its register
file with 9 bit operands that could exceed it; and a self referential jump ran
forever. Counts are now checked against the bytes that remain, nesting is capped
at the limit the reference compiler uses, register access is bounds checked, and
execution runs under a deadline and an instruction budget.
